*.cab
*.msi
*.msix
*.msm
*.msp

# Recorded journal fixtures are committed on purpose and read byte-for-byte in tests
# (architecture.md §8) - the blanket *.log rule above must not swallow them.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.log


# The compiled installer is a build output, not source; the release workflow builds it.
installer/*.exe

# A provider key handed to the scenario suite for one paid run. Never committed, and deleted
# after the run — it exists so a key can reach the process without passing through a transcript.
.paid-key

# The RadioAudition spike writes audition.wav beside the repo root by default. A three-megabyte
# workbench artifact, and one `git add -A` away from being in the history for good — which is
# how it got there once.
/audition.wav

# The Debug build's data folder (D47.App.csproj, DevDataRoot). A running Commander's checklist,
# settings and secrets — never in the history, and deliberately not under bin\ any more, because
# deleting build output used to delete them.
/dev-install/

# ...and the general form of that rule, because the specific one has already gone stale once. The
# folder was renamed dev-data\ -> dev-install\ on one branch and the line above moved with it on
# that branch alone, so on every other branch it named a path that no longer existed and ignored
# nothing. A `git add -A` then swept a Commander's live checklist, settings, secrets and 226 MB of
# Whisper models into a commit on this public repository (2026-08-24); GitHub's large-file hook
# refused the push, for the size rather than for the data, which is not a control this repository
# gets to rely on. A rename must not be able to do that again.
#
# Everything a running d47 writes goes to a folder called data\ beside the executable, wherever
# that executable is (CLAUDE.md, "Everything the app writes goes to data/ beside the executable"),
# so the name is ignored at any depth rather than at one path. Nothing in this repository is
# tracked under a folder of that name and nothing is meant to be. Both install roots are named
# outright as well, so anything a build drops beside data\ - models, audio, captures - is covered
# too.
data/
/dev-install/
/dev-data/

# wrangler's machine-local state from Worker provisioning; never repository material
worker/.wrangler/

# The large hull art (#289). Every hull has three files in assets\ships\: the card still, which is
# committed because it ships inside the download, and a 4K picture and a turntable, which are not.
# Those two are 260 MB across the fleet - they change when somebody re-renders a hull and never
# otherwise, so putting them in history would be permanent, would land in every clone and would be
# paid again by CI on every push. They are published as assets on a pinned GitHub release instead
# and fetched for the hull being looked at; see ShipArtStore.Source for where from, and
# tools\ship-art.ps1, which puts them here on the way out of the render pipeline.
/assets/ships/*.4k.png
/assets/ships/*.spin.mp4
